course: dictionary
lesson: 15616
title: Tat: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To know which one the writer means, look at the words around it: the context. «The shop sells tourist tat.» The word tourist is a clue. Tat means cheap, useless things, the sort of junk sold to visitors at a seaside stall.
explain: «They kept paying each other back: it was tit for tat all afternoon.» The clue is paying each other back. Tit for tat means answering something bad with something bad in the same way. Tat here is not junk at all, because it is part of a phrase.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. Does "cheap, useless things" fit «tourist tat»? Yes, it does. Does it fit «tit for tat»? No, so you know it must be a different meaning.
fact: Tat (noun, informal, UK) means cheap, tasteless or useless things, like junk sold at a fair.
fact: «Tit for tat» means paying someone back in the same way for something bad they did to you.
fact: Tat is also slang for tattoo, and to tat means to make lace by tatting, using a small shuttle and thread.
fact: Tat is an informal word, so you hear it in chatty speech more than in formal writing.
fact: Tit for tat often makes an argument worse, because each side keeps hitting back.
exercise: «The beach shop was full of plastic tat.» What does tat mean here? | Kind, friendly visitors | Sandy towels for the beach | *Cheap, useless things | Very tall buildings
exercise: Mum says, «Don't waste your pocket money on that tat.» What does tat mean? | A gift from a grandparent | Lace made with thread | A tattoo on your arm | *Cheap, tasteless junk
exercise: Ravi and Sam kept hitting back at each other: «It was tit for tat all afternoon.» What does tit for tat mean? | Sharing a bag of sweets | *Paying each other back in the same way | Playing a quiet game | Walking home together
test: «He showed his friends his new tat under his sleeve.» What does tat mean here? | Paying someone back | Cheap, useless things | A piece of lace | *A tattoo, in short slang
test: Tatting is a craft. What does to tat mean? | Paint a picture on skin | *Make lace using a small shuttle and thread | Sell cheap things at a fair | Argue loudly with a friend
exam: Which meaning of tat fits this sentence: «The stall was full of seaside tat»? | Lace made by hand | Paying someone back | *Cheap, useless things | A tattoo
